      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "Using `#[cmse_nonsecure_entry]` on a function limits its capabilities. Namely, only up to 4 32-bit arguments can be accepted, and none of them may be passed on the stack. The same is true for the `\"C-cmse-nonsecure-call\"` ABI.\r\n\r\nCurrently, this is checked in LLVM, so the user experience is sub-par, and the check happens very late (during codegen instead of type checking). It should be checked in rustc instead.",
